{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Sk6gWfeQuyhmNFR8MvZ21D","type":"tool_result","content":"## Bugfixes\n- Handle invalid working directories gracefully when using `--full-path`, see #1900 (@Xavrir).\n- Fire the \"search pattern contains a path separator\" diagnostic for any pattern containing `/`, not just patterns that happen to name an existing directory. Preserves the legacy Windows behaviour that also flags native `\\` separators when the pattern resolves to a real directory. See #1873.\n- Apply the \"search pattern contains a path separator\" diagnostic to patterns given via `--and` as well, not just the primary pattern.\n- Fix bug where passing \"-\" as a directory argument didn't actually search that directory, see #849 (@Sean-Kenneth-Doherty).","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"116c6eef-e10d-4537-a4b7-047da9a0857d","uuid":"12fda2e3-fec2-4a26-a4eb-d3bf7ff415a5","timestamp":"2026-10-18T14:46:55.482Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"## Bugfixes\n- Handle invalid working directories gracefully when using `--full-path`, see #1900 (@Xavrir).\n- Fire the \"search pattern contains a path separator\" diagnostic for any pattern containing `/`, not just patterns that happen to name an existing directory. Preserves the legacy Windows behaviour that also flags native `\\` separators when the pattern resolves to a real directory. See #1873.\n- Apply the \"search pattern contains a path separator\" diagnostic to patterns given via `--and` as well, not just the primary pattern.\n- Fix bug where passing \"-\" as a directory argument didn't actually search that directory, see #849 (@Sean-Kenneth-Doherty).","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/tmp/tlw-vycp0m8v/CHANGELOG.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":7,"oldLines":6,"newStart":7,"newLines":7,"lines":[" ## Bugfixes"," - Handle invalid working directories gracefully when using `--full-path`, see #1900 (@Xavrir)."," - Fire the \"search pattern contains a path separator\" diagnostic for any pattern containing `/`, not just patterns that happen to name an existing directory. Preserves the legacy Windows behaviour that also flags native `\\` separators when the pattern resolves to a real directory. See #1873.","+- Apply the \"search pattern contains a path separator\" diagnostic to patterns given via `--and` as well, not just the primary pattern."," - Fix bug where passing \"-\" as a directory argument didn't actually search that directory, see #849 (@Sean-Kenneth-Doherty)."," "," # 10.4.2"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/tmp/tlw-vycp0m8v/CHANGELOG.md"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Sk6gWfeQuyhmNFR8MvZ21D","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg9tGR9YRrYgvbGECvJbu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"fd now flags path separators in `--and` patterns, not just the main pattern. All tests pass (111 integration, 139 unit). Before this, `fd foo --and one/two` just returned nothing; now it gives the same error the main pattern already got:\n\n```\nThe search pattern 'one/two' contains a path-separation character and will not lead to any search results.\n```\n\nWhat changed:\n\n- **`src/main.rs`:** I moved the separator check into a new helper, `looks_like_a_path`, without changing what it checks. `ensure_search_pattern_is_not_a_path` now runs it on the main pattern and then each `--and` pattern, and names the first one that fails in the error. On Windows, a pattern with `\\` is still only flagged when it names a real directory, so regexes like `\\d+` keep working. `--full-path` still turns the check off for every pattern.\n- **`tests/tests.rs`:** added `test_and_pattern_with_forward_slash_is_rejected`. It checks that `--and one/two` gives the error, and that with `--full-path` the same search runs and returns results.\n- **`CHANGELOG.md`:** added a Bugfixes entry.\n\nClippy reports nothing new. One existing \"redundant reference\" warning went away because I rewrote that code. `cargo fmt` isn't installed here, so I couldn't run the formatter; I formatted the code by hand to match the file.\n\nI haven't committed anything (you're on a detached HEAD). Tell me if you want a branch and a commit."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":383,"cache_read_input_tokens":38982,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":383,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":490,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session